<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chhatrapati</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chhatrapati was the royal title adopted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> at his coronation in 1674, meaning lord of the parasol, a symbol of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. It was held by Shivaji and his successors as rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state. Later, real power in the Maratha Empire passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a>, while the Chhatrapati remained the nominal sovereign.</p></div>
